      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [{ "type": "text", "text": "Hungary and across Central Europe. The original gulyas was made on open fires by cattle herders on the puszta -- the Hungarian plain. Today it is Hungary's most exported dish, found with regional variations in Austria, Czech Republic, Slovakia, and Germany." }]
